WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:00.867
I'm joined tonight

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:01.768
by Maggie Haberman

00:00:01.768 --> 00:00:02.702
of The New York Times,

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.771
also the author of Confidence Man

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.039
The Making of Donald Trump

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:07.841
and the Breaking of America.

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:09.642
Maggie, I mean, Trump is

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:11.277
I feel like we've seen this movie before

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:11.611
where he is

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.146
promising to finally reveal

00:00:13.146 --> 00:00:14.614
something that he has been teasing,

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:15.715
especially the election

00:00:15.715 --> 00:00:16.282
fraud claims

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:17.717
that have never been borne out.

00:00:17.717 --> 00:00:18.918
But you have new reporting on

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:19.753
what's behind

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:21.454
what we're expecting to see on Monday.

00:00:21.454 --> 00:00:23.156
So Jonathan Swan, my colleague

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.858
and I reported earlier today

00:00:24.858 --> 00:00:26.693
that aides and allies of Trump

00:00:26.693 --> 00:00:27.427
woke up this morning

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:27.994
several hours

00:00:27.994 --> 00:00:29.863
after this indictment was filed.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.663
Accusing him

00:00:30.663 --> 00:00:32.665
of trying to subvert the 2020 election

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.933
as part of a conspiracy

00:00:33.933 --> 00:00:34.634
to discover

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:35.702
that he had posted on Twitter

00:00:35.702 --> 00:00:36.036
social,

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.670
saying he has a major news conference

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:38.038
on Monday

00:00:38.038 --> 00:00:39.773
where he's going to release a report

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.341
now that report in question

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.010
turns out to refer to a document crafted

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:46.413
or you know created at least in part

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:48.114
by Liz Herrington, a Trump

00:00:48.114 --> 00:00:49.449
communications aide

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.683
and it refers to Georgia.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.253
And it is going to address what she is,

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:54.120
I think, and whoever

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:54.754
she was working on it,

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.522
we're going to argue,

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:56.856
was widespread fraud.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:57.657
Now, we know those claims

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.626
have been debunked over and over and over

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.361
Brian Kemp, the state's governor,

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.463
again, tried to denounce this today

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.098
and said the election was not stolen.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:06.366
Let's move on.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.033
The reason

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:07.801
the presence of Liz

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.935
Harrington is interesting

00:01:08.935 --> 00:01:10.503
is that she is connected

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:11.571
to a key scene

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:13.540
in the documents indictment

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.809
where Trump is waving around, according

00:01:15.809 --> 00:01:16.976
to prosecutors,

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:18.778
a classified document

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:19.913
or a secret document,

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:20.880
as he refers to it

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:21.781
that he acknowledges

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:24.084
he could have declassified as president.

00:01:24.084 --> 00:01:25.351
And she is one of the women

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.320
quoted in the recording of that.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:29.055
We have been told by multiple sources

00:01:29.055 --> 00:01:31.291
that whether this actually happens

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:32.525
remains to be seen.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.027
So the person who is named

00:01:34.027 --> 00:01:36.229
and one of the other indictments

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:37.030
that is facing him

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.731
is now helping him respond

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.467
to this latest indictment. Correct.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.503
And it speaks to the way that world works

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:43.937
right now.

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:44.871
A number of the people

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.206
who are around him, either

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:48.241
as advisers or as lawyers or,

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:49.742
you know, all kinds of other people

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:51.244
are connected to these cases

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.112
in various ways.

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:54.481
They are witnesses in some cases.

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:54.714
You know,

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.317
Rudy Giuliani is clearly coconspirator

00:01:57.317 --> 00:01:59.452
number one in the federal indictment

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.353
against Trump

00:02:00.353 --> 00:02:02.755
related to January six and trying to

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.457
overturn the election results.

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.059
And he is indicted in Georgia.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:08.561
And so it just creates this

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:09.062
culture

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.131
that we've just never seen before.

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.499
There are so many co-defendants

00:02:12.499 --> 00:02:14.300
listed in this new indictment, which,

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:15.001
I mean, immediately

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:16.269
made me think of the concern

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:17.704
that he has about the potential

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.005
for them to to.

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.840
I mean, there's a lot of opportunities

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.609
for people to cooperate here.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.911
There are. And he is aware of that.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.613
And it is one of the things that

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:27.780
I believe has concerned him

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:28.548
about this indictment.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.183
Also, the fact that it is in state court,

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.885
it is not something he could control.

00:02:31.885 --> 00:02:33.520
If he becomes president again,

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.587
although I think there's an argument

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:34.754
as to

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:35.488
whether a state case

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:36.289
would actually go forward

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.924
against the sitting president

00:02:37.924 --> 00:02:39.325
the way this is.

00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:40.727
But, yes, these are

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:41.895
this is many tentacled.

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:43.396
It's big.

00:02:43.396 --> 00:02:44.697
There are a lot it's the limits.

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:46.299
And there's a lot of allegations in it.

00:02:46.299 --> 00:02:47.534
And there are a lot of people

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:48.301
connected to it,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.303
not all of whom are in his direct orbit.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.638
That's the other thing to bear in mind.

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:51.804
Yeah.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.072
The second half of that list

00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:55.141
is all like Coffee County officials

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:57.210
who aren't directly connected to him.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.344
Mark Meadows is, though,

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.546
I mean, to see his name

00:02:59.546 --> 00:03:00.313
as I was reading through it

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.414
when it first got released last night,

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:03.516
like reading Mark Randall Meadows,

00:03:03.516 --> 00:03:04.284
I mean, just stood out.

00:03:04.284 --> 00:03:05.118
He hasn't been indicted

00:03:05.118 --> 00:03:05.952
in the other cases.

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.954
He's now the first one to try to say,

00:03:07.954 --> 00:03:09.022
well, I was just fulfilling

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:10.723
my official White House duties,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.791
and that's why he's trying to get it

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:13.560
moved to a federal court here.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:14.160
It's an argument

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.261
that I expect that former

00:03:15.261 --> 00:03:16.563
President Trump will make to

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.197
which is that

00:03:17.197 --> 00:03:18.064
they were acting

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.232
under the color of their jobs

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:20.066
and that this is something

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:21.701
that should belongs in federal court

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:22.969
because of that.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.604
I'm not surprised to see Meadows

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.406
make that argument like you

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:27.440
it was

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.875
striking to see his name

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:29.542
in this indictment

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.411
because his name has been at the center

00:03:31.411 --> 00:03:32.912
of this whole issue

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:34.147
as it's been investigated

00:03:34.147 --> 00:03:35.582
for the last two and a half years.

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:36.749
But your correct.

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:37.684
He was not

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.519
one of the coconspirators mentioned,

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:41.120
as best as we could tell, who they were

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:42.622
in the Jack Smith indictment.

00:03:42.622 --> 00:03:44.924
He has not been charged federally.

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.227
He has been much less of a presence

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.395
than we are used to around Donald Trump.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.464
And he is one of the people about whom

00:03:51.464 --> 00:03:52.365
I think

00:03:52.532 --> 00:03:53.333
the former president

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:54.434
is the most concerned

00:03:54.434 --> 00:03:56.169
about what they may or may not have said.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:56.669
Certainly,

00:03:56.669 --> 00:03:58.471
a lot of aides around Trump are concerned

00:03:58.471 --> 00:03:58.771
about what

00:03:58.771 --> 00:03:59.839
he may or may not have said

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:01.474
in various investigations. Yeah.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.809
And also the questions of how

00:04:02.809 --> 00:04:03.876
that affects what Jack

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:04.744
Smith is trying to do.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:06.746
Clearly, if he's trying to use him.

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:07.413
The other thing, you know,

00:04:07.413 --> 00:04:08.581
just reading through the indictment,

00:04:08.581 --> 00:04:09.916
a lot of it is like it's things

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:10.617
that we knew

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:11.918
that had happened or what they did.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:12.785
But also I was just struck

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:16.122
the 12 of the 161 overt acts

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.290
as funny willies referred to

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.659
them were Trump's tweets.

00:04:19.659 --> 00:04:20.260
Yeah.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:20.760
Yeah.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:21.261
And public

00:04:21.261 --> 00:04:22.895
and then others were public statements.

00:04:22.895 --> 00:04:23.129
Yeah.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:25.098
I mean, these are this is

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:26.199
look we talked about this

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.201
a lot with the tweets that they were just

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:29.269
things he was doing.

00:04:29.269 --> 00:04:30.303
There was a joke about,

00:04:30.303 --> 00:04:30.870
you know,

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:32.038
I was about to write a story

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.573
and Trump just tweeted it out. Right.

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:34.474
I mean, this was literally

00:04:34.474 --> 00:04:36.242
they were planning all these actions

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.111
